From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] fix(telos-node): drop duplicate engine.* flags in TelosArgs

TelosArgs previously declared its own `--engine.persistence-threshold`
and `--engine.memory-block-buffer-target` fields. These shadowed the
identical flags in upstream EngineArgs, which caused clap to fail
at runtime with:

    error: the following required argument was not provided:
           persistence_threshold
    Usage: Reth [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

When two `#[arg(long = ...)]` fields share the same long name inside a
single Command, clap silently drops one of the two long attributes and
falls back to treating that field as a required positional argument
(named by the Rust field, hence the underscore). The result is that
even a fully specified command line fails to parse, and the binary
cannot start at all.

Both of the duplicated fields were dead code inside the telos crates
(no call site ever read `args.persistence_threshold` or
`args.memory_block_buffer_target`), so the correct fix is to drop them
entirely and let upstream EngineArgs own those knobs. The third
telos-specific flag, `--engine.max-execute-block-batch-size`, does not
clash with upstream and is kept.

Reproducer: run any telos-reth subcommand with these flags explicitly
set on the command line. Pre-patch, the node exits with status 2 and
the message above before even reaching the `node` subcommand handler.

Signed-off-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/telos/node/src/args.rs | 13 +------------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/telos/node/src/args.rs b/crates/telos/node/src/args.rs
--- a/crates/telos/node/src/args.rs
+++ b/crates/telos/node/src/args.rs
@@ -1,9 +1,6 @@
 //! clap [Args](clap::Args) for Telos configuration
 
-use crate::{
-    DEFAULT_MAX_EXECUTE_BLOCK_BATCH_SIZE, DEFAULT_MEMORY_BLOCK_BUFFER_TARGET,
-    DEFAULT_PERSISTENCE_THRESHOLD,
-};
+use crate::DEFAULT_MAX_EXECUTE_BLOCK_BATCH_SIZE;
 use reth_telos_rpc::telos_client::TelosClientArgs;
 
 /// Telos CLI arguments
@@ -29,14 +26,6 @@ pub struct TelosArgs {
     #[arg(long = "telos.gas_cache_seconds")]
     pub gas_cache_seconds: Option<u32>,
 
-    /// Configure persistence threshold for engine.
-    #[arg(long = "engine.persistence-threshold", default_value_t = DEFAULT_PERSISTENCE_THRESHOLD)]
-    pub persistence_threshold: u64,
-
-    /// Configure the target number of blocks to keep in memory.
-    #[arg(long = "engine.memory-block-buffer-target", default_value_t = DEFAULT_MEMORY_BLOCK_BUFFER_TARGET)]
-    pub memory_block_buffer_target: u64,
-
     /// Maximum number of blocks to execute sequentially in a batch.
     #[arg(long = "engine.max-execute-block-batch-size", default_value_t = DEFAULT_MAX_EXECUTE_BLOCK_BATCH_SIZE)]
     pub max_execute_block_batch_size: usize,
